' coordinates at x=406 rather than on branch ECDL.r, M4's distance_mm on ECDL.r is measured from BS1 (x=125) during the placement pass; setting distance_mm=473 places M4 at x=598 (192 mm after CELL)."}, {"op": "move", "element_id": "M5", "field": "distance_mm", "from": 246.0, "to": 527.0, "note": "distance_mm: 246 \u2192 527 \u2014 Set distance_mm=527 from BS2 (x=125) so M5 is placed at x=652 (246 mm after CELL at x=406), avoiding CELL's footprint and letting probe 2 pass through CELL."}, {"op": "move", "element_id": "BD_PUMP", "field": "distance_mm", "from": 200.0, "to": 560.0, "note": "distance_mm: 200 \u2192 560 \u2014 Increased distance_mm to 560 mm so the counter-propagating pump beam from M8 passes completely through CELL (x=406) before terminating at (307, 165)."}], "rationale": "In the placement pass, M4 and M5 were placed at distance_mm=192 and 246 from BS1 and BS2 (at x=317 and x=371, BEFORE CELL at x=406), so the probe beams folded upward before ever reaching CELL; increasing M4 and M5 distances to 473 mm and 527 mm (and BD_PUMP to 560 mm) places M4 and M5 at x=598 and x=652 after CELL so both probes and the counter-propagating pump traverse CELL cleanly without mount collisions."}

